There are branching maps where the alternative secondary dungeon chain
has an ending floor, It would be a bug (documented) if you could fall
down the _lowest_ floor... it would no longer be an alternative
branch, the dungeon would be a graph with cycles, not a tree, etc.
Dead end corridors are quite common though, and handling them is a
game experience strategy. The player does not have a clear
representation of how the dungeon is structured if he gets lost in
alternative branches...


